m, and the ruthless enemy commander Aphrodia is hungry for vengeance of her own. Can Marin gain the Earthlings' trust, avenge his father, and stop the war?\n\n(Source: Discotek Media)\n\nNote: Originally planned and scripted for 39 episodes, the series was cancelled with various reasons cited including lack of anime magazine coverage and constant airtime changes. The 31st and last episode to air was actually produced as episode 32. Three unaired completed episodes (31, 33, 34) were later released on LaserDisc/DVD/Blu-ray, and the finished scripts and storyboards for the final 5 episodes had been shared in various magazines and a deluxe book."},"tags":[{"name":"Episodic","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"War","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Military","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Space","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Time Manipulation","rank":70,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Aliens","rank":66,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Super Robot","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Guns","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Adult Cast","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Revenge","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Environmental","rank":20,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Tragedy","rank":20,"spoiler":true}],"titles":{"display":"Space Warrior Baldios","english":"Space Warrior Baldios","native":"宇宙戦士 バルディオス","romaji":"Uchuu Senshi Baldios","synonyms":[{"language":"ja","source":"bangumi","value":"宇宙戦士バルディオス"},{"language":"zh","source":"bangumi","value":"宇宙战士巴鲁迪奥斯"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"高达王"}]},"trailer":null,"visibility":"general"}